Hint:\(v=\sqrt{\frac{GM}{r}}\)

Step:Find the ratio of the speeds of the satellites.
The orbital speed of a satellite revolving in a circular orbit is given by;
\(\Rightarrow v=\sqrt{\frac{GM}{r}}\)
The ratio of the speeds of the satellites is given by;
\(\Rightarrow \frac{v_1}{v_2}=\sqrt{\frac{r_2}{r_1}}\)
Substitute the known values we get;
\(\Rightarrow \frac{v_1}{v_2} =\sqrt{\frac{800}{3200}}=\frac{1}{2}\)
